<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">setcondition</ansi> <ansi fg="red">[Admin]</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">setcondition</ansi> command applies a condition (helpful, harmful, or
a status effect such as Bleeding or Cursed) to yourself or to a
player or mob in the room, by its id or by name (a name applies the
first search match).

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

::rows
  <ansi fg="command">setcondition [conditionId]</ansi>  Apply a condition to yourself, by id or name.
  <ansi fg="command">setcondition [target] [conditionId]</ansi>  Apply a condition to a player or mob in the room, by id or name.
  <ansi fg="command">setcondition search [text]</ansi>  Search conditions by name.
  <ansi fg="command">setcondition list</ansi>  List every condition and its id.
::

A condition whose spec stacks (multiple applications building up over
time, such as Bleeding) cannot be applied this way; it can only be
granted by whatever move or effect actually produces it.
